WEBVTT

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.290
This is... the house I
lived in a long time ago.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.620
What is this about, Orpheus?!

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.620
This puzzle has transcended time and space.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.590
It is the Time Maze!

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.830
Change your past and seize...

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.300
the future where you become a Phi-Brain!

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.980
Even If Something’s Missing

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:23.030
If I realized back then that the POG
was keeping an eye on me...

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:31.370
I solved it!

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:38.000
Kaito, it’s dinner time.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:41.310
Hey, Mom! What’s that?

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.390
Huh?

00:02:43.610 --> 00:02:46.300
Orpheus is showing me another
one of his fake pasts...

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.390
No, that’s not right! This is...

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.440
After Mama and Daddy died,
I lived on my own, just like that.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.400
If only I had met Jin sooner...

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.160
Excuse me...

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.700
I seem to have gotten lost.

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.700
Jin! But why?

00:03:08.590 --> 00:03:12.460
Did the past change to
match what I was thinking?!

00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:15.380
I’m sorry, Kaito.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:16.960
Kaito!

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.050
I get it.

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.750
What’s wrong, Mom?

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.870
He wants us to get through this maze

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.280
without letting it consume
our hearts, doesn’t he?

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.930
The puzzle contains...
whatever pasts they desire?!

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.980
Exactly! That is what makes
it the Puzzle of God!

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.730
How am I supposed to go
about solving this puzzle?

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.240
But I have to solve it!

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.260
I must save Jin!

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.850
They were fakes...

00:03:49.370 --> 00:03:51.040
They weren’t my mom and dad...

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:55.750
Mom and Dad didn’t lose their lives, but...

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.740
Are you sure?

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:02.340
Didn’t you love them?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:04.800
Are you sure you want to
let them go over this?

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:05.800
Raetsel?!

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.840
Kaito Daimon!

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:12.680
Kaito Daimon’s past is
overlapping with mine.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:17.110
It’s a promise!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.650
I’m holding you to this promise!

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:29.950
I can’t believe we’re going on a
journey with Kaito Daimon!

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:37.280
Did Raetsel wish for this past?

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:39.540
Or did I...?

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.160
I solved it, Jin!

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:52.720
So did I! Lookie!

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.980
Oh! You two are good!

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.920
This feels nostalgic.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.980
I don’t care to change the past anymore,

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.650
but I wish we coulda hung out
with Jin like that forever...

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.080
Jin, you look like you truly
are enjoying yourself...

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:16.730
Jin!

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:17.580
Jin!

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:25.130
That’s right. Throughout our journey,
Jin was always suffering in agony...

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:28.780
I didn’t know...

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:34.140
I’ve never seen Jin suffer like that over
solving a puzzle, not even once.

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:34.890
Here.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.650
No fair! You gotta give me something!

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:44.900
I’ll give you something next time, Kaito.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:48.270
Why not now?! I want something!

00:05:45.670 --> 00:05:50.560
If we continued to travel like this,
Jin would never have left me...

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.220
Jin! Kaito!

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:54.870
Huh?

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:55.790
What is it?

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:02.420
Will the three of us be together
forever, just like this?

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.590
Huh? Of course we will!

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:09.260
Yeah! We’ll be together forever, Raetsel!

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.520
Right, all three of us...

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.070
Raetsel, this is where we part ways.

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:28.820
Why are you leaving, Jin?!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:31.570
Is he going to solve the Puzzle of God...?!

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:34.580
Is he leaving to battle Count Pythagoras?!

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:37.660
Kaito, you’re coming with me.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:39.670
No!

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:42.680
J-just me?

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:47.020
I want you to see this
through to the end, Kaito.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.510
Take me with--

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:49.320
Raetsel!

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:56.210
You’re missing something,
so I can’t risk taking you.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.600
Jin, why would you say such a thing?!

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:04.150
I don’t want this past! Why am I seeing it?

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.230
Let’s go, Kaito.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.320
But...

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:09.190
Wait, Jin.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:14.160
Why, Jin?

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:18.100
Raetsel, has the past consumed your heart?!

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.250
You’re leaving me behind again...

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.750
How dare you abandon me...!

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:29.260
Pull yourself together, Raetsel!

00:07:29.750 --> 00:07:31.170
I won’t accept this...

00:07:31.600 --> 00:07:33.510
I won’t accept this!

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.180
Raetsel!

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:41.770
What happened?!

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:44.000
I’m all the way back here again!

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.020
What’s going on?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:49.530
Are you sure?

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.070
Raetsel!

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:57.410
I get it! She plans on redoing her past!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:58.690
Starting here!

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.920
Raetsel, this is where we part ways.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.930
You’re missing something.

00:08:16.340 --> 00:08:17.430
You’re missing something.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.180
You’re missing something!

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:20.930
You’re missing something!

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:22.690
You’re missing something!

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.150
No!

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:32.020
You need to stop, Raetsel!

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:37.830
Jin, what the heck is Raetsel missing?!

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:38.820
Here.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:43.560
What’s this?

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.210
My good luck charm.

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.140
I’d like you to keep it from now on.

00:08:48.140 --> 00:08:50.340
When I’m challenging a Puzzle of Fools...

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.590
Not good! At this rate,
it’s going to consume me!

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:01.010
Raetsel, you’re missing something.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:02.980
Raetsel!

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.680
No! No, no, no!

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:08.810
I will NEVER accept that!

00:09:14.270 --> 00:09:15.190
Not again...

00:09:15.190 --> 00:09:16.240
We’re back here again!

00:09:18.530 --> 00:09:19.420
Are you sure?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.910
Didn’t you love them?

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:24.290
Are you sure you want to
let them go over this?

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.000
Raetsel vanished?!

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:47.760
Good morning...

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:49.390
Good morning!

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.220
Good morning.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.830
What is this all about?!

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:01.870
Her desire to reject that bitter memory

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:05.450
has caused Raetsel to deviate
from the flow of time.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:08.750
She has deviated from the flow of time?

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.460
Raetsel is no longer in
one of the past worlds.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:17.710
She is in a fabricated world that she
created to protect her own mind.

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:19.800
Her heart has been completely consumed.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:23.160
No one can contact her there.

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:27.600
Likewise, it is impossible for her to ever come back.

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:31.270
Then that would make this
puzzle’s winner...

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.440
Kaito Daimon.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.440
Wanna tag along?

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.280
You could come with me.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:47.410
You have a gift with puzzles.

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.740
What’s goin’ on?

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:53.170
Doesn’t this Jin know about Raetsel?

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:56.360
Have you been traveling by
yourself this whole time?

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:57.540
Yeah, that’s right.

00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:02.220
That’s why I’d like a talented
partner such as yourself.

00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:06.810
Does this mean Raetsel chose a
past where she never met Jin?!

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:09.560
Come on! Let’s go together.

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.520
Kaito!

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:14.820
I had a kinda weird dream.

00:11:15.190 --> 00:11:17.100
A dream? What was it about?

00:11:18.850 --> 00:11:20.130
I don’t remember.

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:22.610
More importantly, did you fill that out?

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.280
Fill what out?

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.070
The questionnaire about your future plans.

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:27.870
Didn’t you say it was due today?

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:31.960
What? You still haven’t filled it out?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:37.460
It’s nice that you’re carefully
considering your future, but...

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:38.710
I’m sorry.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.720
Our student-teacher meeting is next week,

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.800
so make sure to submit it
before then. Sound good?

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:44.720
Yes.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:51.720
I wrote that I wanted to go on to college.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.230
I put that I wanna be a nurse!

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:55.520
How about you, Miss Erena?

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:57.980
I think I really do want to become a model...

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:02.370
Actually, I’ve already sent
my resume to an audition!

00:12:02.690 --> 00:12:04.090
Awesome!

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:07.880
Miss Raetsel, is there
anything you’d like to do?

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.000
Raetsel, you’ve always been like this.

00:12:13.550 --> 00:12:19.450
You get top grades, excel in sports,
and could have any guy you wanted!

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:21.870
But you always seem so bored.

00:12:21.870 --> 00:12:24.510
That’s not... actually true.

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.510
Manager!

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:33.270
Hey, Erena! Quit chitchatting
and come hit the track.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:35.730
Yeah, yeah! I know the drill.

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:38.510
The track team has practice during lunch?

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:40.490
Only when a tournament is coming up!

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:44.780
I’m not about to let victory escape
us as long as I’m the captain!

00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.280
Later! I’ll see you around.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.030
Uh-huh.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.850
I collected the data on all of our opponents.

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.450
What?! You’re done already?

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.040
Way to go, Cube!

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.550
Mr. Gammon and Miss Erena!

00:12:56.550 --> 00:13:00.240
Isn’t the romance between a
captain and his manager nice?

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:02.800
Someday Mr. Jikukawa and
I will be a couple...

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:06.240
But I don’t think you
should date your teacher...

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:09.490
I won’t confess how I feel
until after graduation!

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:22.820
I wonder what I like...

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.320
What do I want to do?

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:37.160
Kaito Daimon hasn’t moved from
that location for a while now.

00:13:40.790 --> 00:13:41.590
He moved!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.240
Excuse me!

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:20.170
Here. Didn’t you solve
it just the other day?

00:14:20.660 --> 00:14:23.410
It’d be sad if you threw it away.

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:24.960
How do you figure?

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:28.960
Well, don’t you like puzzles?
Isn’t that why you solve them?

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:31.440
It’d be sad if you threw it
away even though you like it...

00:14:32.490 --> 00:14:33.640
It’s revenge.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.180
I will solve all of the puzzles in the world.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.140
That is my revenge.

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.600
Your revenge...?

00:14:57.410 --> 00:14:59.290
Is that another puzzle?

00:15:00.910 --> 00:15:03.460
Looks fun! Let me try my hand at it.

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:04.000
H-hey!

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:07.760
I’m Raetsel. And you are?

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.520
It’s nice to meet you!

00:15:30.030 --> 00:15:33.880
Amazing! It’s almost like a secret fort.

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:39.790
What made you start following me around?

00:15:41.290 --> 00:15:44.060
The way you were playing
with puzzles... I guess.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:45.040
Puzzles?

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.300
I thought they seemed fun.

00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.790
Nothing else has ever struck me that way before.

00:15:52.920 --> 00:15:54.340
I wonder why...

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:27.090
How to Make Puzzles

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:26.670
Kaito...

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.840
Kaito... Daimon...

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:28.890
All of them are missing something...

00:17:28.890 --> 00:17:31.310
Nuh-huh. They aren’t missing anything!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.480
Uh, but...

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.690
Aren’t these paintings incomplete?

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:39.280
Nuh-huh! They’re all done.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:41.490
Everything is missing something!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.720
Same for people!

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:49.790
Everyone is missing something.
We’re lacking something or other.

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:51.800
And that’s just fine!

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:56.800
So there is no need to try
and fill those holes in.

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.970
If you do, they’ll just get bigger.

00:17:59.970 --> 00:18:02.310
If you try to draw closer,
they’ll just go farther away.

00:18:02.660 --> 00:18:03.970
Isn’t it strange?

00:18:14.730 --> 00:18:16.940
Everyone lacks something...

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:05.410
Kaito!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:10.080
Why did you take off without telling me?

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:13.260
Was I getting in your way?

00:19:13.260 --> 00:19:14.090
No.

00:19:14.420 --> 00:19:15.540
Then why...?

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:19.590
My mom and dad weren’t my real parents.

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:23.350
They belonged to a certain organization

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:27.720
and were teaching me how to solve
puzzles to achieve some goal.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.530
Is that why you’re getting
back at the puzzles?

00:19:31.390 --> 00:19:32.890
Even now, I’m scared.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:36.190
Scared someone is going to betray me again.

00:19:36.980 --> 00:19:39.860
Is that why you’ve been living by yourself?

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:43.430
Is that why you tried to leave me?

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.870
I was starting to enjoy the puzzles.

00:19:49.450 --> 00:19:51.270
I used to loathe them,

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:56.290
but when I solve puzzles with
you, they’re kinda fun...

00:19:56.790 --> 00:19:59.210
I started to lose sight of myself...

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.890
I can understand that.
I was having fun myself.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:07.080
The truth is that you like puzzles, Kaito!

00:20:10.900 --> 00:20:14.520
You know, I thought I didn’t
want to do anything.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:18.060
Or that I didn’t like anything at all.

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:23.320
I was afraid that maybe
I was missing something.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:25.490
But I had fun...

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.700
It’s okay if I’m missing
something, isn’t it?

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:33.210
Even if I’m lacking,
I still had a good time.

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:36.590
I genuinely enjoyed myself.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.320
Where am I? Where have I been...?

00:20:55.270 --> 00:20:59.300
You got completely absorbed
into that fake world.

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.610
Did you come to my rescue?

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:05.500
How?!

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:07.990
I knew the normal method wouldn’t work.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:12.260
So I thought super hard that
I wanted to take a path

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:14.120
that I’d never follow in the real world.

00:21:15.060 --> 00:21:17.120
And that method worked!

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:19.630
It’s a path you’ve never taken before?

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.460
I didn’t go with Jin.

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:26.970
Did you actually chose me over Jin?!

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.740
After going through a life
where I didn’t choose Jin,

00:21:30.740 --> 00:21:32.850
I understood how you felt for the first time.

00:21:33.780 --> 00:21:36.150
Spending your life hating
the thing you loved...

00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:40.020
Getting abandoned by the
person you believed in...

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:42.380
It’s really painful.

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:45.650
Let’s ask Jin what he meant when he
said you’re missing something!

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:48.780
And while we’re at it,
let’s give him a piece of our minds!

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:55.410
The real Kaito Daimon appeared inside
of Raetsel’s fabricated world?!

00:21:55.700 --> 00:21:58.820
I thought you said no one could reach her!

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:01.890
After placing himself in the same situation,

00:22:01.890 --> 00:22:04.420
he drew close to Raetsel’s psyche.

00:22:05.210 --> 00:22:07.030
Sure enough, you are fascinating...

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.640
Kaito Daimon!

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:18.940
Wh-what’s going on?!

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:25.990
Raetsel!

00:22:26.480 --> 00:22:28.740
Raetsel!

00:24:03.290 --> 00:24:05.380
Jin, thank you.

00:24:05.980 --> 00:24:11.750
Everything you taught me through puzzles,
Jin, is still alive inside of me.

00:24:12.300 --> 00:24:14.510
So please rest at ease.

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:18.420
No matter what happens, I swear
I will protect the future!

